# Part VI: Revised Research Program — Phases

## Phase 0: Epistemic Audit
- Convert every existing proposition from both conversations into typed claims (13-field format)
- Remove unjustified "if and only if" language
- Separate laws, definitions, assumptions, conjectures, values
- Build the dependency graph with typed inference edges
- Apply the six failure signatures (IV.11) as self-diagnostic
- Run the six boundaries on the program itself (IV.10)

## Phase 1: Stereo Generation
- Track A: Typed claims downward from scoped postulates
- Track B: Regularities upward from pre-specified case/data corpus (Ostrom, Bettencourt, Rockström, paleoclimatic collapses, historical persistences, non-Western knowledge systems)
- No shared language forced yet
- **Track B must include systems that do not share the axiom set** (IV.4)

## Phase 2: Contradiction Mining
- Agreement / over-deduction / missing mechanism / genuine contradiction
- Contradictions become the research queue; they are not filled
- Force at least one mapping into a low-prestige domain (IV.7)

## Phase 3: Grounding
- Every surviving claim gets a world-hook (presently available referent) and a typed falsifier
- Toy model whose outputs can surprise the authors (mandatory)
- All three adversarial checks (IV.5.2) — historical case, analogical paraphrase, statement of limitation
- Claims that fail go back or die
- Pre-register proxy indicators that stand or fall with the claim

## Phase 4: Formal Validation
- Executable semantic validation checklist (IV.6.1)
- Heterogeneous verification routing (IV.6.2)
- Compositional autopsy: derive one joint prediction no unit made; check for hidden forbiddings; if none possible, the composition is vacuous — delete layers until it isn't

## Phase 5: Resistance-Landscape Survey
- Re-generate the same layer under two alien analogical frames and one altered postulate
- Keep the intersection

## Phase 6: Branch-Point Map
- All policy families sit at marked forks
- Each fork names the measurement that closes it
- No "central ratio" unless Phase 3 has made it a quantity
- Publish the branch points, not a verdict

## Phase 7: Empirical Confrontation
Start with bounded systems where stocks, flows, and governance are measurable: fisheries, aquifers, watersheds, regional nutrient cycles, electricity systems, urban water systems. Do not begin with "civilization as a whole."

## Phase 8: Method Validation
Randomize theory-building tasks across:
1. Ordinary prompting
2. Original ULU prompting
3. Typed proof-carrying claim units
4. Claim units + external verification (heterogeneous routing)
5. Full pipeline (Phases 0–7)

Blind evaluators score: factual error, contradiction rate, unsupported inference, unit errors, novelty, correction cost, reproducibility.

